tasks.body:
Goal:
- Build and qualify the complete integrated source before any target-branch update.

Touch:
- Current solution, Functions, all three Workers, relevant hydrated UI journeys, PWA lifecycle and release evidence.

Implementation constraints:
- Preserve canonical task identities, stopped checkpoints, original receipts, secrets and per-account consent. No force push, destructive reset, automatic history rewrite, live gameplay test, independent-user acceptance or backlog implementation.
- The preceding integration task supplies the scoped recipes. Run Worker suites separately from .NET and other Worker suites. Use synthetic providers and exact source/build identity. Repair actual merge defects and rerun affected checks; stale original receipts never establish current integrated acceptance. Physical-device and actual-account qualification remain separate.

Validation:
```json
{
  "checks": [
    {
      "id": "integrated-dotnet",
      "recipe_id": "release-dotnet",
      "criteria": [
        "The integrated source passes all current .NET and Functions controls with nonzero discovery, zero required skips and preserved original failures."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "Habitica.sln",
        "tests/release/qualification.py"
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "report_directory": ".skill-tree/history/validation/integrate-production/dotnet"
      },
      "assertion": "The integrated source passes all current .NET and Functions controls with nonzero discovery, zero required skips and preserved original failures.",
      "timing": "before-dependent-work"
    },
    {
      "id": "integrated-workers",
      "recipe_id": "release-workers",
      "criteria": [
        "All three matching Worker bundles build and the complete synthetic Auth and Workspace suites pass without provider effects or weakened assertions."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "workers/release-inputs.json",
        "tests/release/qualification.py"
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "report_directory": ".skill-tree/history/validation/integrate-production/workers"
      },
      "assertion": "All three matching Worker bundles build and the complete synthetic Auth and Workspace suites pass without provider effects or weakened assertions.",
      "timing": "before-dependent-work"
    },
    {
      "id": "integrated-browser",
      "recipe_id": "release-browser",
      "criteria": [
        "Current Release browser qualification verifies affected shared and task flows, light/dark phone/desktop enlarged text, native storage and service-worker lifecycle with owned cleanup."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "src/Habitica.WebApp/wwwroot/service-worker.published.js",
        "tests/release/qualification.py"
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "report_directory": ".skill-tree/history/validation/integrate-production/browser"
      },
      "assertion": "Current Release browser qualification verifies affected shared and task flows, light/dark phone/desktop enlarged text, native storage and service-worker lifecycle with owned cleanup.",
      "timing": "before-dependent-work"
    }
  ]
}
```

Acceptance:
- The integrated source passes all current .NET and Functions controls with nonzero discovery, zero required skips and preserved original failures.
- All three matching Worker bundles build and the complete synthetic Auth and Workspace suites pass without provider effects or weakened assertions.
- Current Release browser qualification verifies affected shared and task flows, light/dark phone/desktop enlarged text, native storage and service-worker lifecycle with owned cleanup.

Goal:
- Publish the complete main release to the existing production site and matching services, then verify source identity and operational readiness.

Touch:
- Cloudflare Pages habitica-companion, existing Auth/MCP/Workspace Workers, migration preflight, public plugin artifacts and release records.

Implementation constraints:
- Preserve canonical task identities, stopped checkpoints, original receipts, secrets and per-account consent. No force push, destructive reset, automatic history rewrite, live gameplay test, independent-user acceptance or backlog implementation.
- The owner explicitly authorizes production publication and necessary additive migrations. Inspect actual deployed resources, preserve consent and runtime capabilities, retain recovery bookmarks and exact predecessor versions, and avoid irreversible account/key operations. Validate the stable origin after any Git-connected build and keep a concrete release/rollback handoff.

Validation:
```json
{
  "checks": [
    {
      "id": "production-identity",
      "recipe_id": "release-hosted",
      "criteria": [
        "Production serves the exact complete main application and coherent matching Workers with required migrations, existing runtime settings and recoverable predecessor identities."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "deploy/coordinated-release.py",
        "tests/release/qualification.py"
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "report_directory": ".skill-tree/history/validation/integrate-production/hosted"
      },
      "assertion": "Production serves the exact complete main application and coherent matching Workers with required migrations, existing runtime settings and recoverable predecessor identities.",
      "timing": "before-dependent-work"
    },
    {
      "id": "production-browser",
      "recipe_id": "release-hosted-browser",
      "criteria": [
        "Hosted routed cold startup and PWA/storage smoke checks pass on the deployed artifact, with device/account paths truthfully reported as separate review limits."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "tests/release/hosted-smoke.mjs",
        "src/Habitica.WebApp/wwwroot/service-worker.published.js"
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "report_directory": ".skill-tree/history/validation/integrate-production/hosted-browser"
      },
      "assertion": "Hosted routed cold startup and PWA/storage smoke checks pass on the deployed artifact, with device/account paths truthfully reported as separate review limits.",
      "timing": "before-dependent-work"
    }
  ]
}
```

Acceptance:
- Production serves the exact complete main application and coherent matching Workers with required migrations, existing runtime settings and recoverable predecessor identities.
- Hosted routed cold startup and PWA/storage smoke checks pass on the deployed artifact, with device/account paths truthfully reported as separate review limits.
